 ```
 
+For a controlled source-mixture trial, `--archive-source-weights weights.json`
+accepts a JSON object mapping every nonempty resolved archive path to a positive
+presentation weight. Weights are normalized independently of archive sizes.
+Each training batch draws seeded multinomial source quotas and cycles each
+source through its own shuffled blocks. This preserves other sources' exact
+sampled rows in matched trials that replace one source (with the same batch,
+seed, source ordering and per-epoch budget below both corpora's row counts).
+History records actual admitted per-source presentations, including tails.
+Holdout still enumerates every reserved record once. Checkpoints bind the
+normalized mixture contents on resume. Omitting this option keeps the existing
+block-permutation sampler.
+
 Pass disjoint held-out shard globs with `--validation-data` to log a full
 float32 validation loss after every epoch. Validation uses the same filters
 and objective, includes the final partial batch, and never updates weights.
